{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0097194","isObsolete":false,"name":"execution phase of apoptosis","definition":{"text":"A stage of the apoptotic process that starts with the controlled breakdown of the cell through the action of effector caspases or other effector molecules (e.g. cathepsins, calpains etc.). Key steps of the execution phase are rounding-up of the cell, retraction of pseudopodes, reduction of cellular volume (pyknosis), chromatin condensation, nuclear fragmentation (karyorrhexis), plasma membrane blebbing and fragmentation of the cell into apoptotic bodies. When the execution phase is completed, the cell has died.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"21760595"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"apoptosis","type":"narrow"},{"name":"execution phase of apoptotic process","type":"exact"}],"children":[{"id":"GO:1900119","relation":"positively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:1900118","relation":"negatively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:0070782","relation":"part_of"},{"id":"GO:0006921","relation":"part_of"},{"id":"GO:1900117","relation":"regulates"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-12-05","action":"Added","category":"XREF","text":"Reactome:R-HSA-75153"},{"timestamp":"2024-03-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-11-08","action":"Deleted","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-11-08","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2023-11-01","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044763 (single-organism cellular process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0009987 (cellular process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-05-01","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"has part GO:0006915 (apoptotic process)"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-12","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A stage of the apoptotic process that starts with the controlled breakdown of the cell through the action of effector caspases or other effector molecules (e.g. cathepsins, calpains etc.). Key steps of the execution phase are rounding-up of the cell, retraction of pseudopodes, reduction of cellular volume (pyknosis), chromatin condensation, nuclear fragmentation (karyorrhexis), plasma membrane blebbing and fragmentation of the cell into apoptotic bodies. When the execution phase is completed, the cell has died."},{"timestamp":"2014-04-12","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A stage of the apoptotic process that starts with the controlled breakdown of the cell through the action of effector caspases or other effector molecules (e.g. cathepsins, calpains etc.). Key steps of the execution phase are rounding-up of the cell, retraction of pseudopodes, reduction of cellular volume (pyknosis), chromatin condensation, nuclear fragmentation (karyorrhexis), plasma membrane blebbing and fragmentation of the cell into apoptotic bodies. The execution phase ends when the cell has died."},{"timestamp":"2012-12-15","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0009987 (cellular process)"},{"timestamp":"2012-12-15","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044763 (single-organism cellular process)"},{"timestamp":"2012-12-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"apoptosis"},{"timestamp":"2012-11-22","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"execution phase of apoptotic process"},{"timestamp":"2011-11-26","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A stage of the apoptotic process that starts with the controlled breakdown of the cell through the action of effector caspases or other effector molecules (e.g. cathepsins, calpains etc.). Key steps of the execution phase are rounding-up of the cell, retraction of pseudopodes, reduction of cellular volume (pyknosis), chromatin condensation, nuclear fragmentation (karyorrhexis), plasma membrane blebbing and fragmentation of the cell into apoptotic bodies. The execution phase ends when the cell has died."},{"timestamp":"2011-11-26","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"execution phase of apoptosis"},{"timestamp":"2011-11-26","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0006915 (apoptotic process)"},{"timestamp":"2011-11-26","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0009987 (cellular process)"}],"xRefs":[{"dbCode":"Reactome","dbId":"R-HSA-75153"}],"annotationGuidelines":[{"description":"Annotating cell death and apoptosis using the new guidelines","url":"https://wiki.geneontology.org/index.php/Apoptosis_Curation_Manual"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0097194","ancestorName":"execution phase of apoptosis","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"4896","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Schizosaccharomyces pombe"},{"ancestorId":"GO:0097194","ancestorName":"execution phase of apoptosis","relationship":"only_in_taxon","taxId":"33154","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Opisthokonta"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted","blacklist":[{"goId":"GO:0097194","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000315 from this reference: PMID:3470709","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"P01137-PRO_0000033762","taxonId":"9606","entityName":"TGFB1_HUMAN","ancestorGoId":"GO:0006915"},{"goId":"GO:0097194","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000266 from this reference: GO_REF:0000121","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"P17246","taxonId":"10116","entityName":"TGFB1_RAT","ancestorGoId":"GO:0006915"},{"goId":"GO:0097194","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000314 from this reference: PMID:11870224","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"P52803","taxonId":"9606","entityName":"EFNA5_HUMAN","ancestorGoId":"GO:0006915"},{"goId":"GO:0097194","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual a